.TH LT-QWWAD_EF_DONOR_GENERIC "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_ef_donor_generic (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_ef_donor_generic \- find state of electron orbiting a donor ion in a heterostructure using a generic search.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_ef_donor_generic
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find state of electron attached to a donor in a 2D system using a generic search
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.HP
\fB\-e\fR [ \fB\-\-dcpermittivity\fR ] arg (=13.18) Bulk relative permittivity
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-mass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Bulk effective mass (relative to free
electron)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR [ \fB\-\-particle\fR ] arg (=e)
ID of particle to be used: 'e', 'h' or
\&'l' for electrons, heavy holes or light
holes respectively.
.TP
\fB\-\-subband\fR arg (=1)
Principal quantum number of subband for
which to find impurity state.
.TP
\fB\-\-impuritystate\fR arg (=1s)
Symmetry of impurity state (1s, 2s, 2px,
or 2pz)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR [ \fB\-\-donorposition\fR ] arg
Location of donor ion [Angstrom]
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Input files:
   'v.r'         Confining potential for heterostructure:
                 Column 1: position [m].
                 Column 2: potential [J].

   'wf_*i.r'     Wave function amplitude at each position:
                 Column 1: position [m]
                 Column 2: wave function amplitude [m^{-1/2}].

.SS Output files:
   'E*.r'        Energy of each state:
                 Column 1: state index.
                 Column 2: energy [meV].

   'l.r'         Bohr radius of ion:
                 Column 1: Dopant location (from r_d.r file) [Angstrom]
                 Column 2: Bohr radius [Angstrom]
   
   'searchlog.r' Log of the search algorithm progress:
                 Column 1: Bohr radius [m]
                 Column 2: Energy [J]

In each case, the '*' is replaced by the particle ID and the 'i' is replaced by the number of the state.
The zeta.r file is only created if a variable symmetry waveform is used.
.SH EXAMPLES

Find the 2s eigenstate for a donor at z = 10 Angstrom:
    qwwad_ef_donor_generic --donorposition 10 --impuritystate 2s

Find the 2px eigenstate for a donor at z = 100 Angstrom, for the 2nd principal subband:
    qwwad_ef_donor_generic --donorposition 100 --impuritystate 2px --subband 2
.SH "IMPURITY STATE OPTIONS"
This program provides several different options for the symmetry of the dopant orbit.
This can be selected using the --impuritystate option, and may take the values: '1s', '2s', '2px' or '2pz'.
